  "rawText": "Global United Trading LLC logo\n\nGlobal United Trading LLC\n\nShare\n\nShow more options\n\nData Engineer\n\nEbina, Kanagawa, Japan · 3 months ago · Over 100 applicants\n\nPromoted by hirer · Actively reviewing applicants\n\n On-site\n\nMatches your job preferences, workplace type is On-site.\n\n Full-time\n\nMatches your job preferences, job type is Full-time.\n\nEasy Apply\n\nSave\n\nSave Data Engineer at Global United Trading LLC\n\nData Engineer\n\nGlobal United Trading LLC · Ebina, Kanagawa, Japan (On-site)\n\nEasy Apply\n\nSave\n\nSave Data Engineer at Global United Trading LLC\n\nShow more options\n\nYour profile is missing required qualifications\n\nShow match details\n\nBETA\n\nIs this information helpful?\n\nAbout the job\n\nCompany Description\n\nGlobal United Trading operates and manages an e-commerce website that offers quality Japanese genuine and performance parts to customers around the world. We do our best to provide an exceptional experience to customers who are looking to order parts directly from Japan and we were successful to achieve this since the company’s establishment in 2015. Our services are highly recommended by our customers and we seek to maintain such position as the company continues to grow year over year. Consequently, to maintain our market growth, we are looking for a data engineer that will assist us in expanding and maintaining our products catalogue as well as enhancing our operations and market insights.\n\nRole Description\n\nThis is a full-time on-site role for a data engineer at our Ebina office. As a data engineer, the role will be to create, update, and delete data on the website to keep the website information up to date and to expand our market coverage and product catalogue. The role will also include analyzing available data to improve daily operations and gain useful market insights.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDevelop data pipelines to get the latest product updates from various manufacturers websites.\n\nData extraction from various document types that are provided by the manufacturer.\n\nPerform data processing, cleansing and formatting. \n\nIntegrate data pipelines with our system to realtime updates.\n\nCollaborate closely with the customer in design and development of the software\n\nPrepare technical documentation.\n\nQualifications\n\nExcellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\nAbility to work effectively both independently and in a team environment\n\nRequirements:\n\nWeb scraping experience\n\nData modeling experience\n\nExperience with API programming.\n\nFamiliarity with different relational databases like SQLite and Postgres\n\nFamiliarity with Git and GitHub.\n\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or relevant data engineer experience.\n\nExcellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n\nAbility to work effectively both independently and in a team environment\n\nBusiness level English. \n\nGreat to have:\n\nExperience with ML/DL modeling and programming.\n\nFlask programming experience.\n\nGraphQL API programming experience.\n\nExperience using data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI)\n\nWorking Hours:\n\nMonday-Friday 09:00-18:00 \n\nVacation/holidays:\n\nSaturdays, Sundays, and holidays\n\nNew year holiday season\n\nAnnual paid leave\n\nWork location:\n\nEbina City, Kanagawa Prefecture\n\nAccess:\n\nAbout 8 minutes on foot from Odakyu Line, Sotetsu Line Ebina Station\n\nAbout 10 minutes on foot from JR Sagami Line Ebina Station\n\nTreatment/Benefits:\n\nTransportation expenses (maximum 30,000 yen/month) When using public transportation\n\nVarious social insurance (as required by law)\n\nAnnual paid vacation (as required by law)\n\nSalary:\n\n3.8M-4.2M per year (Depending on performance)\n\nOthers: \n\nTrial period of 3 months\n\nEmployment Type: Full-Time Employee\n\nAbout the company\n\nGlobal United Trading LLC company logo\n\nGlobal United Trading LLC\n\n{:followerCount} {:followerCount}\n\nFollow\n\nRetail  2-10 employees  8 on LinkedIn\n\nFounded in 2015, Global United Trading was born in Yamato city near Tokyo, Japan. The goal is to provide a bridge that directly connects customers from around the world to suppliers in Japan thus eliminating border and language barriers.\n\nThe company started by supplying customers with aftermarket and custom car parts through eBay and expanded to establishing the our own branded website that is visited by many customers everyday day.\n\nThe company is currently also expanding to software development, logistics and preowned car export to further answer to customer’s needs and requests.\n\nWe are currently looking for top talents to work together to further expand the companies current and future business and to further reach customers from around the world.\n\n…\n\nshow more\n\nShow more"
  }
}
